    "created_at": "2026-08-13T18:30:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-13T18:30:58Z",
    "body": "https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-color/system-color-consistency.html?label=experimental&label=master&aligned to me tests something useful. It asserts that when a browser supports a system color that can be used in CSS by web developers, that they can be assured that browsers themselves use the same value. It would be weird to me if a `LinkText` is exposed to web developers with a particular color and then browsers use a different color for text in links.\r\n\r\nIf I understand your comment correctly, you would like to see an additional test that asserts particular values for specific system colors? That would mean we have 1 test that asserts `LinkText` is `#0000EE` and then 1 test that asserts that both the text of an `<a>` and `LinkText` have the same value (ergo text in `<a>` also has color `#0000EE`).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
